%% M6 required sequence: courier status update -> Kafka -> tracking-service -> Socket.IO -> browser.
%% Source of truth: contracts/events/parcel-status-changed.v1.schema.json, contracts/openapi/tracking-service.v1.yaml
%% (server event parcel.status), doc/01-architecture.md section 5.3.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor CO as Courier
    participant P as parcel-service
    participant OB as Outbox relay
    participant K as Kafka<br/>parcel.status-changed.v1
    participant TC as ParcelStatusChangedConsumer
    participant DB as MongoDB<br/>tracking.timelines
    participant SG as Socket.IO gateway<br/>/ws/tracking
    participant RD as Redis adapter
    actor CU as Customer browser<br/>live timeline
    actor GU as Guest browser<br/>/track/TRACKING_NO

    CO->>P: PATCH /api/v1/courier/parcels/{id}/status OUT_FOR_DELIVERY
    P->>P: TX: update parcel, insert history row, insert outbox row
    P-->>CO: 200 OK
    OB->>K: publish ParcelStatusChanged, key = parcelId
    K-->>TC: deliver (one partition per parcelId, so order is kept)
    TC->>TC: validate envelope against JSON Schema
    TC->>DB: is eventId in processed_events?
    alt duplicate eventId (at-least-once redelivery)
        TC-->>K: commit offset, no change
    else new event
        TC->>DB: TX: push event, set currentStatus, refresh publicView, insert processed_events
        TC->>SG: emitStatus(rooms: tracking:TRACKING_NO, user:CUSTOMER_SUB, user:MERCHANT_SUB, dispatch)
        SG->>RD: publish to adapter channel
        RD-->>SG: fan out to sockets on every replica
        SG-->>CU: emit parcel.status (owner payload)
        SG-->>GU: emit parcel.status (masked payload only)
        TC-->>K: commit offset
    end
    Note over CU,GU: Target: the page updates within about 1 second, with no refresh
